  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that multiprofile multimodal (config_018, acc=0.619) dramatically outperforms singleprofile multimodal (config_016, acc=0.527), a +9.2% jump driven by the multiprofile setting with avgpool aggregation. The only untested dimension within this best-performing family is the aggregation method: we have only seen avgpool. Config_020 changes exactly one variable (aggregation: avgpool → transformer) while holding all else constant (pca_n2000, resnet50, concat fusion, multiprofile). This directly tests whether a more expressive aggregation (transformer, which can model inter-profile relationships) can further improve over the simple average pool, or whether the gain from multiprofile is already captured by averaging. Under a limited budget, this clean single-variable ablation on the most impactful design axis (how multiple profiles are combined) maximizes information gain: a positive result opens a high-performing direction, while a null/negative result confirms avgpool suffices and redirects effort toward other levers (fusion strategy, image encoder)."
